        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "HOWARD L. BOLTER, ESQ., Minneapolis, Minnesota; on behalf of the Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 00-1514, Lance Raygor and James Goodchild v. the Regents of the University of Minnesota. Mr. Bolter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Howard L. Bolter",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1367 is a constitutional and sensible response by Congress to the serious procedural problems that were facing the Federal courts prior to 1990."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What -- what's wrong with, as some courts did, conditioning dismissal upon -- upon the plaintiff's -- upon the defendant's agreement to -- to waive the statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bolter",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In that situation with -- with two States, I would say that unless it was within the time period of California, it would probably not be tolled in that situation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. Well, that -- that seems to me very similar to what we have here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bolter",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They didn't make, as a part of that condition, anything about tolling. That's -- that's I think the -- the first point, and -- and that's what this statute is doing, is tolling. It's not changing that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Bolter, what you said might be so if the only purpose of the statute of limitations were repose, being notified on time that you're subject to suit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know of any case in which this Court has held that Congress, when passing a statute of its own, could totally forbid a State to enact a similar statute?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bolter",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm not aware of a case like that, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rotenberg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The statute is unconstitutional if the Court needs to address the question of legislative power, Justice Stevens, because there is no case upholding a congressional power to enact a sweeping expansion of statute of limitations --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rotenberg",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Breyer, I agree with you that Alden does not compel a particular interpretation of State law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Rotenberg, because sovereign immunity is kind of a peculiar objection -- that is, the State -- it's up to the State to waive it or not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0002-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROTENBERG: 20 days, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When this Court confronts a general grant of jurisdiction, like 1367(a), it routinely infers that the statute does not apply to nonconsenting States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Howard L. Bolter",
      "case_id": "2001-00-1514",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0ff0be7a027f79e9c148b37a79e447f79e80e19dc2d8532ceeef460d3b2dbfa",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0ff0be7a027-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is -- their arguments -- the -- the university and the Solicitor General's arguments rely on the fact that they were a nonconsenting State throughout this whole procedure. And that's not an accurate characterization of what went on here."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
